To separate distributions of the top $m$-th and top $(m+1)$-th machine, as shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:random}(b), all we need is the following $\omega_0$:
\begin{eqnarray}
\omega_0  & = & \frac{\gamma^{\prime}}{2 - \gamma^{\prime}} , \\
\gamma^{\prime} & = & P_{(m)} + P_{(m+1)}
\end{eqnarray} 
Here, $P_{(m)}$ denotes the top $m$-th reward probability.
In fact, for $M$-machine and $X$-player cases, we have designed a physical system that can  determine the overall optimal state, called the ``social maximum,'' quickly and accurately~\cite{bom}.

